  OCR TREND ANALYSIS — IS OCR → 1 JUSTIFIED?
========================================================================

    n |      OCR |    1-OCR |    1/n | (1-OCR)*n |      trend
  -------------------------------------------------------
    3 | 1.000000 | 0.000000 | 0.3333 |    0.0000 | EXACT (OCR=1)
    4 | 1.000000 | 0.000000 | 0.2500 |    0.0000 | EXACT (OCR=1)
    5 | 0.969925 | 0.030075 | 0.2000 |    0.1504 | (1-OCR)*n = 0.1504
    6 | 0.959056 | 0.040944 | 0.1667 |    0.2457 | (1-OCR)*n = 0.2457
    7 | 0.958107 | 0.041893 | 0.1429 |    0.2933 | (1-OCR)*n = 0.2933

  IF OCR = 1 - c/n, then (1-OCR)*n should be CONSTANT.
  IF OCR = 1 - c/n², then (1-OCR)*n should DECREASE.

  (1-OCR)*n for n≥5: ['0.1504', '0.2457', '0.2933']
  INCREASING → OCR converges SLOWER than O(1/n)
  The claim 'OCR → 1 at rate O(1/n)' may be WRONG!

